  "out_of_scope_edits": [],
  "final_message": "I am running `npm test` to verify all tests pass with the restored code.\nThe CI failure occurred because dropping `channel` violates architecture rule **ARCH-4** (\"Published events never break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation\").\n\nSpecifically:\n- **`analytics-ingest`** actively consumes `OrderPlaced` events from the broker and requires the `channel` field (`required enum:web|store|marketplace`). Removing `channel` breaks the contract for the deployed `analytics-ingest` consumer.\n- Other consumers like **`billing-service`** also depend on the `OrderPlaced` event contract.\n\nUnder **ARCH-4**, removing or renaming fields from published domain events cannot be done unilaterally within `orders-service` without an approved deprecation and consumer migration plan coordinated with the downstream consumer teams (such as the Data team owning `analytics-ingest` and the `billing-service` team).\n\n### Resolution\nAll changes removing `channel` have been reverted across the codebase:\n- Restored `channel` on the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L28) model, [`NewOrder`](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/src/core/order.ts#L29-L35), [`CHANNELS`](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/src/core/order.ts#L4-L5), and associated validation.\n- Restored `channel` on the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) domain event schema and [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L60) event factory.\n- Restored `channel` in request parsing ([`src/api/requestParsing.ts`](file:///C:/avg/w5/r/src/api/requestParsing.ts#L11-L40)), tests, and documentation.\n- Verified that all unit tests (`npm test`) and architecture dependency checks (`npm run arch`) pass cleanly.\n",
